{
  "dom_id": "step-q66758",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "${log}_{4}⁡(16{x}^{3})=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, the given expression can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡(16{x}^{3})={log}_{4}⁡16+{log}_{4}⁡({x}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $16={4}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{4}⁡16={log}_{4}⁡({4}^{2})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡(16{x}^{3}) & ={log}_{4}⁡16+{log}_{4}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+{log}_{4}⁡({x}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
